<section class="home-top">
  <h1 class="home-title">Open the box<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></h1>
  <p class="home-sub">Three real systems running where you can poke them: a Huffman compressor, a key-value store that writes to disk, and a packet network that routes with Dijkstra. Change the input and watch them work.</p>
</section>

<section class="boot" aria-label="Modules">
  <div class="boot-screen" id="boot">
    <div class="boot-line dim">sysplay bios v2.0, (c) 2026 Janat Yasser</div>
    <div class="boot-line dim">memory check .......................... 640K ok</div>
    <div class="boot-line">probing modules</div>
    <div class="boot-line">  [ <span class="ok">ok</span> ] <span class="amber">U1</span>  huffman encoder ........... <a href="/compression">./compression</a></div>
    <div class="boot-line">  [ <span class="ok">ok</span> ] <span class="amber">U2</span>  key-value store ........... <a href="/database">./database</a></div>
    <div class="boot-line">  [ <span class="ok">ok</span> ] <span class="amber">U3</span>  packet router ............. <a href="/network">./network</a></div>
    <div class="boot-line">3 modules ready. pick one.</div>
    <div class="boot-line boot-prompt">$</div>
  </div>
</section>
<script>
  // type the boot log out line by line (shown all at once with reduced motion)
  (function () {
    if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    const lines = [...document.querySelectorAll('#boot .boot-line')];
    lines.forEach((l) => (l.style.visibility = 'hidden'));
    lines.forEach((l, i) => setTimeout(() => (l.style.visibility = 'visible'), 180 + i * (i < 3 ? 260 : 340)));
  })();
</script>

<section class="bom">
  <h2>man sysplay</h2>
  <table class="bom-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Ref</th><th>Part</th><th>What you can do with it</th><th>What it teaches</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="ref">U1</td>
        <td><a href="/compression">Huffman compression</a></td>
        <td>Type any text and watch the tree get built merge by merge, then see every character's new code and how many bits you saved.</td>
        <td>Greedy algorithms, priority queues, variable-length codes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="ref">U2</td>
        <td><a href="/database">Key-value store</a></td>
        <td>Drive a real store from a terminal with PUT, GET, DELETE and SCAN. Every write lands in a JSON file on disk.</td>
        <td>Hash indexes, persistence, why range scans need sorted storage</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="ref">U3</td>
        <td><a href="/network">Packet network</a></td>
        <td>Send packets across three topologies, cut a cable mid-run and watch the routes heal, turn up packet loss and count what gets through.</td>
        <td>Shortest-path routing, TTL, packet loss, redundancy</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
